# ── Supabase ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 1. Create a project at https://supabase.com (free tier is plenty).
# 2. Run supabase/schema.sql in the project's SQL editor.
# 3. Copy Project Settings → API → "Project URL" and the "anon public" key
#    into a file named .env.local (git-ignored), using the two names below.
#
# Vite only exposes variables prefixed with VITE_ to the browser. The anon key
# is safe to ship to the browser — Row-Level Security (see the schema) is what
# actually protects each user's data, not the secrecy of this key.
#
# Leave these blank and the app falls back to on-device storage (no accounts,
# no sync, no community library) — handy for local UI work without a project.

VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
